Build the qlog streaming sources into picoquic-core.

picoquic-core's configuration and socket-loop code (picoquic_create_and_configure,
picoqmux_create_and_configure, picoquic_server_set_context) call
picoquic_set_qlog, which is declared in picoquic/picoquic_qlog.h but was
compiled into picoquic-log (loglib/qlog_fns.c). picoquic-log links
picoquic-core, so core could not name log as a dependency without a cycle:
a shared picoquic-core failed to link on Apple, and on ELF it carried the
reference unresolved, so a consumer that links only core -- or links log but
uses none of its symbols under --as-needed -- failed to link, and
BUILD_LOGLIB=OFF left core unusable.

qlog_fns.c and the frame formatter it uses, qlog_frames.c, need only
picoquic-core, picotls and the C library, and nothing else in picoquic-log
calls them except autoqlog.c. Both now build into picoquic-core (CMake and the
Visual Studio projects), with no source change; picoquic-log keeps linking
picoquic-core and gets them from there. Their symbols move from the log
library to the core library.

Applies to picoquic 55b473e207e436d06ea9a2895cc1fc555d42c81c.

